From baaf0bc36739292f79774b75828dc66e5578cbb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:52:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add SampleHz, a sampling profiler for ARM64EC under Wine
 (default off)

Each emulated thread gets a timer on its own CPU time that sends it SIGPROF.
The unixlib handler records the interrupted PC and the thread's last JIT block
header and RIP in a lock-free ring. A FEX-internal thread drains it every
100 ms, maps the host PC back to the exact guest instruction when it is inside
the block (Context::DecodeSampledRIP), names guest and host addresses by
module, offset and nearest export, and once a minute appends the busiest
thread's top 200 and the other threads' top 50 to
/dev/shm/fex-<pid>-samples.csv, with handler and reader cost rows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
